  "_doc": "IMAT paper blueprints. Two fixed variants (MBA harder, BS lighter). Sections VARC, DILR, QA. A group with kind != 'none' shares one stimulus across all its questions (a SET -> one platform config, consecutive). kind 'none' groups are singletons (each question independent). difficulty is a distribution {level: count} summing to size. 'flex': true marks the pool the ±5% --count delta is absorbed into (its medium bucket). 'tita_flex': true marks the TITA pool whose size may be set anywhere in tita_range via --tita (compensated by the QA MCQ pool so the section count holds). Either DILR table or graph sets are allowed in either variant. Difficulty levels are FIXED per variant and must never change; only the flex-pool sizes move.",
